// Unlocking a Mutex that nothing holds is caught where it is cheap to catch:
// the unlock swaps in 'unlocked' and sees that it already was, so it panics,
// as sync's other program errors do. Its .exit is a panic's, the status the
// Microsoft C library's 'abort' ends a program with, 0xC0000409. Its stderr,
// unchecked here since it names a line of sync.cone, which moves as sync.cone
// changes, says: panic at sync.cone:<line>: sync: Mutex.unlock of a Mutex
// that is not locked. What the program printed before is kept: a panic
// flushes stdout first.

mod badunlock;

import stdio use *;
import sync use *;

fn main() {
  imm m = Mutex.make();
  m.lock();
  m.unlock();
  printStr("a lock and its unlock are fine\n");
  m.unlock();
  printStr("never printed\n");
}
